## Workflow overview

harness-maker provides 7 atomic stages and fused workflows.
Invoke a stage by mentioning the skill name (e.g. `@hm-execute task-slug`).

### Atomic stages

| Skill | Purpose |
|-------|---------|
| `@hm-research` | Multi-source fact-gathering; writes RESEARCH doc |
| `@hm-spec` | Acceptance-criteria specification; writes SPEC doc |
| `@hm-plan` | Phase decomposition + ADRs; writes PLAN doc |
| `@hm-execute` | TDD implementation driven by PLAN; no commits |
| `@hm-review` | Deep code review; grades A–F; writes REVIEW doc |
| `@hm-verify` | Full check suite: tests + lint + type |
| `@hm-wrapup` | Final tests, drift gate, single commit |

### Autoloop

| Skill | Purpose |
|-------|---------|
| `@hm-loop` | Bounded autoloop: interview → iterate workflow → wrapup |

### Fused workflows (stages chained in one turn)

| Skill | Chain |
|-------|-------|
| `@hm-exec-rev` | execute → review |
| `@hm-exec-rev-wrap` | execute → review → wrapup |
| `@hm-exec-rev-wrap-ver` | execute → review → wrapup → verify |

Default per-iteration workflow: `@hm-{{ config.default_workflow }}`.

## Configuration

- `harness.yaml` — worktree scope, loop settings, reviewer list
- Worktree isolation: `{{ config.worktree.scope | join(', ') if config.worktree is defined and config.worktree.scope is defined else 'execute' }}`
- Reviewers: {{ config.reviewers.verbosity | default('standard') }} verbosity

## Quality bar

All stage skills carry their own procedures. Each skill is self-contained —
you do not need to read AGENTS.md to execute a stage; invoke the stage skill
directly and follow the embedded procedure.

